FAQ

What is InP optoelectronics?
InP optoelectronics refers to optical and optoelectronic devices manufactured using indium phosphide semiconductor technology.

Why is InP important for optical communications?
InP supports high-performance optical devices such as lasers and photodetectors and is particularly useful for telecommunications and high-speed optical communication applications.

What applications use InP optoelectronic devices?
Applications include optical communications, data centers, telecommunications networks, photonic systems, optical sensing, and other high-speed communication technologies.

